(LIB-11 -- a bare name (no `./`, `../`, or leading `/`) checks
 `/usr/share/vox/lib/<name>` first, falling back to the containing file's
 directory only if that path does not exist. /usr/share/vox/lib does not
 exist in this environment (only /usr/share/vox/coreasm does), so this
 probe only hand-verifies the fallback half: a bare
 "fixtures/libmathkit.lib" still resolves against this file's own
 directory. The precedence half needs write access to
 /usr/share/vox/lib, which requires root -- not verified, see the ledger
 Report. Also covers LIB-12: the trap is the same mechanism, just no
 collision was constructed here.
